# ledger-signing-key.pub — generate your own cosign public key; there is no placeholder.
# Install the public half at $TRAUST_CONFIG_HOME/ledger-signing-key.pub:
#
#     cosign generate-key-pair            # writes cosign.key + cosign.pub
#     mv cosign.pub  <deployment config dir>/ledger-signing-key.pub
#     # keep cosign.key + its passphrase in your secret store; the harness
#     # reads them via LAAS_SIGNING_KEY_PATH / COSIGN_PASSWORD (docs/signing.md)
#
# Record the key's SHA-256 SPKI fingerprint OUTSIDE the repo that holds it:
#
#     openssl pkey -pubin -in ledger-signing-key.pub -outform DER | openssl dgst -sha256
#
# Algorithm: ECDSA P-256 (cosign / Sigstore). Never re-sign historical layers on
# rotation — keep the retired public key alongside as ledger-signing-key-<date>.pub.
